module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.FiniteTypeReflector
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.GlobalSectionsKoszulDerivedLimit
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.KoszulPerfectDual
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.SheafifiedCechFiniteType
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The Koszul formula for the derived completion along a sheaf of ideals of finite type, Tag 0A0E

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site, let `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` be a sheaf of ideals of finite type and let
`E ∈ D(𝒪)`. [Stacks, Tag 0A0E] computes the derived completion `E^∧` of [Stacks, Tag 099F] by
the Koszul complexes on the powers of generators of `ℐ`:

`E^∧ = R lim (E ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 K_n)`,  `K_n = K(𝒪, g_1^n, …, g_s^n)`.

The right-hand side is built from a finite family of sections generating `ℐ`, which a finite-type
sheaf of ideals carries only **locally**; so the formula is proved here over each object `U` of
`𝒞` on which such a family exists, where it reads

`E^∧|_U = R lim (E|_U ⊗^𝐋_{𝒪_U} K_n(g))`,  `g_1, …, g_s ∈ Γ(U, 𝒪)` generating `ℐ|_U`.

The objects carrying such a family cover the site
(`RingedSite.exists_coversTop_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal_of_isFiniteType`), which
`exists_coversTop_isDerivedLimit_koszulPowerSystem_derivedCompletion` below records. For an `ℐ`
generated by finitely many *global* sections the formula holds on `𝒞` itself, and that is the
source's own display,
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_completion`
of `KoszulPerfectDual.lean`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletionOverIsoCompletionFunctor`: **the restriction of
  the derived completion along `ℐ` to a slice on which `ℐ` is generated by finitely many
  sections is the Čech completion of the restriction at those sections**, i.e.
  `E^∧|_U ≅ R𝑆heafHom_{𝒪_U}(Č(g), E|_U)`.

## Main results

* `RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_derivedCompletion_over`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0A0E] at a sheaf of ideals of finite type.**
* `RingedSite.exists_coversTop_isDerivedLimit_koszulPowerSystem_derivedCompletion`: the same,
  packaged with a covering family of objects on each of which the Koszul tower is defined.

## The argument

Three inputs from the library, composed; nothing is assumed.

1. `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletionIsoFiniteTypeCech` of
   `FiniteTypeReflector.lean` identifies the derived completion functor of [Stacks, Tag 099F]
   with `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(K, -)` for the complex `K ⟶ 𝒪` of [Stacks, Tag 099E],
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.finiteTypeCech`.
2. `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctorOfComplexOverIso` — [Stacks, Tag 08JB] —
   restricts that to the slice over `U`, as `R𝑆heafHom_{𝒪_U}(K|_U, E|_U)`; and
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isGlobalExtendedCech_finiteTypeCech` identifies `K|_U` with the
   extended alternating Čech complex `Č(g)` in `D(𝒪_U)`, which is the defining property of `K`
   in [Stacks, Tag 099E]. Together these give
   `derivedCompletionOverIsoCompletionFunctor`: `E^∧|_U` is the Čech completion of [Stacks, Tag
   099B] on the slice at the family `g`.
3. That Čech completion is a derived limit of the Koszul tower, by the source's own display at a
   globally generated ideal sheaf — here on the ringed site `(𝒞/U, 𝒪_U)`, where `g` is a family
   of *global* sections. Transporting a derived limit along an isomorphism of its object is
   `CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsDerivedLimit.of_isoObj`.

## Implementation notes

The derived completion is the reflector `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletion` of
[Stacks, Tag 099F] — the `K^∧` the source's statement refers to — and not the Čech functor of
[Stacks, Tag 099B]; the two are identified by step 1, which is where the finite-type hypothesis
is used, through [Stacks, Tag 099E]. The hypothesis is the source's own, and the only one: no
`Limits.HasProduct` or `Limits.HasCoproduct` argument is carried, the countable products coming
from `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.hasProductsOfShape_nat_derivedCategory_ringSheaf` (K-injective
resolutions) and the countable coproducts from
`Stacks.Injectives.hasCoproducts_derivedCategory`, both made available in this file.

The derived category is pinned with `CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard` at a raised
priority: that is the instance [Stacks, Tag 0A0E] is stated with in `KoszulPerfectDual.lean`, and
at the default priority the two spellings of the derived category of a slice are found with
different `Hom` universes, which makes the composite of step 2 fail to typecheck.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0E)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08JB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08JB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099E)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0913](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0913)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

attribute [local instance 100000] HasDerivedCategory.standard
attribute [local instance] hasProductsOfShape_nat_derivedCategory_ringSheaf

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
  (I : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))
  [I.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType]

/-- **The derived completion along a sheaf of ideals of finite type, restricted to a slice on
which the ideal sheaf is generated by finitely many sections, is the Čech completion of the
restriction at those sections**:

`E^∧|_U ≅ R𝑆heafHom_{𝒪_U}(Č(g_1, …, g_s), E|_U)`

for `g_1, …, g_s` sections of `𝒪` over `U` generating `ℐ|_U`.

The derived completion is the reflector of [Stacks, Tag 099F]. It is `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(K, -)` for the
complex `K ⟶ 𝒪` of [Stacks, Tag 099E] (`derivedCompletionIsoFiniteTypeCech`); derived internal
Hom commutes with restriction to a slice by [Stacks, Tag 08JB]
(`completionFunctorOfComplexOverIso`); and `K|_U` is `Č(g)` in `D(𝒪_U)`, which is the property
defining `K` (`isGlobalExtendedCech_finiteTypeCech`). The last isomorphism is not canonical — it
is chosen from the existential statement of [Stacks, Tag 099E] — which is why this is a
definition rather than a natural transformation. -/
def derivedCompletionOverIsoCompletionFunctor (U : X.C) {s : ℕ}
    (g : Fin s → Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over U).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))
    (hg : idealOfGlobalSections (X.over U) g = overIdeal I U)
    (E : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :
    (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj
        ((derivedCompletion X I).obj E) ≅
      (completionFunctor (X.over U) g).obj
        ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u}
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj E) :=
  (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u}
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.mapIso
      ((derivedCompletionIsoFiniteTypeCech X I).app E) ≪≫
    completionFunctorOfComplexOverIso X U (finiteTypeCech X I) E ≪≫
      ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor (X.over U)).mapIso
        (isGlobalExtendedCech_finiteTypeCech X I U s g hg).choose.op).app
          ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u}
            (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj E)

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0A0E] at a sheaf of ideals of finite type.** Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site, let
`ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` be a sheaf of ideals of finite type and let `E ∈ D(𝒪)`. Let `U` be an object of `𝒞` and
`g_1, …, g_s` sections of `𝒪` over `U` generating `ℐ|_U`. Then the derived completion `E^∧` of
[Stacks, Tag 099F] satisfies

`E^∧|_U = R lim (E|_U ⊗^𝐋_{𝒪_U} K_n)`,  `K_n = Hom_{𝒪_U}(K(𝒪_U, g_1^{n+1}, …, g_s^{n+1}), 𝒪_U)`,

the derived tensor products of `E|_U` with the duals of the Koszul complexes on the positive
powers of `g_1, …, g_s`.

The Koszul complexes of the formula are formed from a finite family of sections generating the
ideal sheaf, and a finite-type `ℐ` carries one only locally; the objects `U` that carry one cover
the site, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_coversTop_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal_of_isFiniteType`,
and `exists_coversTop_isDerivedLimit_koszulPowerSystem_derivedCompletion`
below states this formula over such a covering family. When `ℐ` is generated by finitely many
global sections of `𝒪` the formula holds on `𝒞` itself; that is the source's own display,
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_completion`.

Three inputs, each proved: the identification of the reflector of [Stacks, Tag 099F] with
`R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(K, -)` for the complex of [Stacks, Tag 099E]; the restriction of that to the slice
over `U` as the Čech completion of [Stacks, Tag 099B] at `g`, which is
`derivedCompletionOverIsoCompletionFunctor`; and the source's display on the ringed site
`(𝒞/U, 𝒪_U)`, where `g_1, …, g_s` are global sections. -/
@[stacks 0A0E "the stated formula `K^∧ = R lim (K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 K_n)` for the derived completion of \
`K ∈ D(𝒪)` along a sheaf of ideals `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` **of finite type**, with `K^∧` the derived completion \
functor of [Stacks, Tag 099F] and `K_n` the Koszul complex on the powers of generators of `ℐ` in \
the cochain grading of the source's proof, that is the `𝒪`-dual of \
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulPowerComplex`. The tower of the formula is built from a \
finite family of sections generating `ℐ`, which a finite-type ideal sheaf carries over the \
objects of a covering family, so the formula is stated over each object `U` carrying such a \
family `g_1, …, g_s`, where it reads `K^∧|_U = R lim (K|_U ⊗^𝐋_{𝒪_U} K_n(g))`; that those \
objects cover the site is \
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_coversTop_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal_of_isFiniteType`\
. `R lim` is a predicate rather than a functor, so the source's equality is read as the \
restriction being a derived limit of the tower. The finite-type hypothesis is the source's own, \
and the only one: the countable products and coproducts a derived limit needs in order to be \
written down are supplied here rather than assumed. The source's display at an ideal sheaf \
generated by finitely many global sections of `𝒪` is the companion registration \
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_completion`\
."]
theorem isDerivedLimit_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_derivedCompletion_over
    (U : X.C) {s : ℕ}
    (g : Fin s → Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over U).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))
    (hg : idealOfGlobalSections (X.over U) g = overIdeal I U)
    (E : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :
    IsDerivedLimit
      (tensorDerivedDualSystem (X.over U)
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.canonicalDerivedTensorProduct (X.over U))
        (koszulPowerSystem (X.over U) g ⋙ DerivedCategory.Q)
        ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u}
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj E))
      ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u}
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj
        ((derivedCompletion X I).obj E)) :=
  IsDerivedLimit.of_isoObj (derivedCompletionOverIsoCompletionFunctor X I U g hg E).symm
    (isDerivedLimit_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_completion (X.over U) g
      ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u}
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj E))

/-- **The Koszul formula of [Stacks, Tag 0A0E] holds over a covering family of objects**, for a
sheaf of ideals of finite type: there is a family `{V_i}` of objects covering the final object of
`𝒞` such that over each `V_i` finitely many sections of `𝒪` generate `ℐ|_{V_i}` and, for every
`E ∈ D(𝒪)`, the restriction `E^∧|_{V_i}` is a derived limit of the Koszul tower of those
sections.

This is
`isDerivedLimit_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_derivedCompletion_over` applied to the
covering family of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_coversTop_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal_of_isFiniteType`,
and it carries no attribute: the per-object statement above is the formula, and this records that
the objects it speaks about exhaust the site. -/
theorem exists_coversTop_isDerivedLimit_koszulPowerSystem_derivedCompletion :
    ∃ (ι : Type u) (V : ι → X.C), X.J.CoversTop V ∧
      ∀ i : ι, ∃ (s : ℕ) (g : Fin s →
          Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over (V i)).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u})),
        idealOfGlobalSections (X.over (V i)) g = overIdeal I (V i) ∧
          ∀ E : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)),
            IsDerivedLimit
              (tensorDerivedDualSystem (X.over (V i))
                (Stacks.SheafOfModules.canonicalDerivedTensorProduct (X.over (V i)))
                (koszulPowerSystem (X.over (V i)) g ⋙ DerivedCategory.Q)
                ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u}
                  (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) (V i)).mapDerivedCategory.obj E))
              ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u}
                (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) (V i)).mapDerivedCategory.obj
                ((derivedCompletion X I).obj E)) := by
  obtain ⟨ι, V, hV, hgen⟩ := exists_coversTop_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal_of_isFiniteType X I
  refine ⟨ι, V, hV, fun i => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨s, g, hg⟩ := hgen i
  exact ⟨s, g, hg.symm, fun E =>
    isDerivedLimit_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_derivedCompletion_over X I (V i) g
      hg.symm E⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
